_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fixes #6026\n\n## What\n\nThe Atlas content versioning + retention design doc — #6026's \"Done looks like\" — at `doc/2026-11-08T10-26-00Z_design_atlas_content_versioning_retention/`:\n\n- **Version object model** (§2): `file_id` vs `(file_id, version_seq)` identity (paths are version attributes, never identity), immutable versions, content stored once by hash, lineage edges (`edit` / `rename` / `split` / `merge` / `tombstone`) as first-class evidence-carrying rows, and chunks bound to versions by **occurrence** — so retention can never orphan a chunk a surviving version still points at.\n- **Lineage rules per source type** (§3): Atlas computes and stores its own edges. Git records no renames (per-diff `-M50%` heuristic re-guess), so git's output is one ingestion signal among several (segment/shared-chunk scoring, basename priors); rename-only commit hygiene is a hint-quality lever, not a correctness requirement. Non-git sources anchor on source-native ids or content-neighbourhood inference.\n- **Retention** (§4): per-class table (code / docs / session logs / chat logs / generated reports) with the three triggers parameterized per class — **by date, by increments, by access** (the access trigger consumes the per-version surfaced record from the #6018 stats/feedback design). Governed by the #3125 reconciliation: default keep; a version retires only when a trigger fires **and** its class rule permits; retirement is report-first (dry-run, #6041) and leaves a tombstone record.\n- **Cold rollout** (§6): hot → cold (rustfs) preserves resolvability — cold is a latency class, not a visibility class; deletion is the only hard end. PITR boundary kept per PR #6269: Turso PITR is whole-DB disaster recovery, never a retention mechanism.\n- **Query-side contract** (§5): newest-resolution as a query-time **view** (never destructive replace), tombstone heads do not resurface the previous version, `version` pinning and `as_of` parameters (with #5774/#5755), one-file-best-version hit grouping, and full-version logging per run feeding the query-trace design (#6027).\n- **Implementation split** (§8): storage/lineage and the query contract as new follow-ons under #6018; the retention engine and cold tier fold in the already-filed #6041 and #6042 rather than duplicating them.\n\nDesign only; no implementation is authorized by the doc. Inputs are the settled ones from task 12445's triage verdict on #6026 — nothing re-litigated.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796725670&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7636&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F7636&signature=ea787277bf67f675303f096dbc8aadd72948b08aa96f1f7a9544ddc7435238f0\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/7636?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-08T10:27:47Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T11:11:05Z","closed_at":"2026-11-08T11:11:03Z","merged_at":"2026-11-08T11:11:03Z","merge_commit_sha":"86b8b7be37911b4bd41a6eb9242a3cf8b63e4879","assignee":